Hi,
I am resuming the conversation here because I need additional help.

In my CJS model, z state can take 1 (uninfected), 2 (infected) or 3 (dead). I tried to set up a nimbleFunction to accommodate the ifelse statement that worked in JAGS but not in NIMBLE. But I get an error message about variable name conflict.

 for (i in 1:N){
    # Define latent state at first occasion

    z[i, f.state[i]] <- y[i, f.state[i]]

    # Indicator variable with 0 or 1 if infection is absent or present

    Infection=matrix(NA,length(N),length(n.occasions-1))

    indicatorvarfstate=nimbleFunction(
    run=function(z){
    for (i in 1:(dim(z)[1])) {
       for (j in 1:(dim(z)[2])){
         if (z[i,j] == 2) {
            Infection[] <- 1
    } else {
            Infection[] <- 0
    }}
        return(Infection)
    }})

    Infection=indicatorvarfstate(z)

Defining model
ERROR : Found variable name that conflicts with C++ keywords: if, return. Please use a different name.

