I'm wondering if anyone has any further suggestions for me regarding dmnorm(), and whether anyone else has encountered this problem in the past year. Since my previous posts, I have updated my old Intel MacBook Pro to the latest system, reinstalled R, Rstudio, Xcode, and Nimble. I always have the same problem: R crashes anytime I run a model using dmnorm(). Other models (without dmnorm) seem to work fine, but I really need the multinormal distribution. I have tried writing my own "dmymnorm" and "rmymnorm" Nimble functions (using dmnorm_chol, see above), which work by themselves, but when included in a model the result is the same as using dmnorm.
I'm hoping when I eventually upgrade my computer to a newer Mac, this problem will go away. So far it's a huge mystery.
