Hi Michael,

Hmm, that is frustrating.

I see that your underlying BLAS linear algebra library is the Mac's vecLib BLAS. Usually that is a good idea for efficiency, but I wonder if using R's built-in BLAS would avoid the problem. Did you set up the use of Accelerate BLAS for R yourself, or was that done automatically somehow? (I think users usually have to do that themselves.)

If you did it yourself, I'd suggest temporarily switching back to R's default BLAS.

If you didn't do it yourself, there is some info here <https://cran.r-project.org/bin/macosx/RMacOSX-FAQ.html#Which-BLAS-is-used-and-how-can-it-be-changed_003f> (though I think the paths are slightly different on your machine than in their instructions) on how to switch, and I can provide more help if you run into problems.

-chris

