Thanks for your prompt response!

I did not change BLAS myself.

I have tried changing BLAS in the past, but I'm not sure I'm doing it right. As I understand it, it should be possible to make the switch by changing what the libRblas.dylib link points to, either libRblas.0.dylib, or libRblas.veclib.dylib. With a new installation of R (which is what I have at the moment), in the folder
/Library/Frameworks/R.framework/Resources/lib  (this is where R says to look)
libRblas.lib links to libRblas.0.dylib (R's own BLAS, as I understand it). Changing it back and forth has no effect on what R's sessionInfo() reports (and no effect on my crashing problem).
I remember coming across some online discussion about this, explaining why this change does not show up (something about how newer versions of macOS work), but I didn't understand it. When I go to the directory which shows up in the R sessionInfo(), i.e.
/System/Library/Frameworks/Accelerate.framework/Versions/A/Frameworks/vecLib.framework/Versions/A
there is no BLAS library (or any lib file) there at all, so it seems I am missing something.
BTW, I also looked in the directory
/Library/Frameworks/R.framework/Versions/4.4-x86_64/Resources/lib
which is where sessionInfo() says libRlapack.dylib is located. That directory also has libRblas.dylib pointing to libRblas.0.dylib.

cheers,
Michael O'Dell

